          },
          {
            "skills": ["skill:crafting"]
          },
          {
            "skills": ["skill:religion"]
          }
        ],
        "casters": 1
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "066064db-b5b9-5cd1-b94d-c86672f68a3d",
    "pack": "tian-xia-world-guide",
    "kind": "ritual",
    "slug": "ritual:seed-of-mercy",
    "name": "Seed of Mercy",
    "level": 3,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["trial"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "tian-xia-world-guide"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The gods who value benevolence and the caretaking of small and vulnerable beings also value those qualities in the mortal adventurers who journey through the lands of Tian Xia. You demonstrate your willingness to aid even the most helpless of life by nursing a small, injured bird to health and allowing it to fly away to freedom, earning in return the protection of the natural world. If you're able to nurse the bird to health, it will return to you with a seed, which will grow into a sprout bearing a single flower."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sprout withers if you don't personally water it with at least 1 Bulk of pure spring water a day or if it's left unattended in dangerous circumstances. It's anathema to this ritual to let the sprout wither, and doing so immediately ends its benefits. If the ritual is ended in this way, you must conduct an Atone ritual before attempting this ritual again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " As success, except the sprout also grows a single fruit after you've cared for it for a week. Removing the fruit causes the sapling to wither, but the fruit can be eaten as a "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "afe38f9f-9558-511f-8f33-724d5c8c5718",
            "label": "Moderate Healing Potion"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You nurse the bird to health. It returns to you with a seed that, when planted and watered, grows into a sprout with a single flower. Once you've cared for it for a week, you gain the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "d21fd9b4-22f0-5dd9-980e-fd02482e0bcf"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " feat. If you lose Toughness due to violating the ritual's anathema, you lose a number of Hit Points equal to the decrease in your maximum Hit Points."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You aren't able to heal the bird, but you help its passing to be as painless as possible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your attempt to heal the bird causes greater suffering. Another bird brings you a seed that, if planted, will grow into a gourd that releases a small demon to attack you."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.opXqASAY37ltENB8"
    },
    "data": {
      "rank": 3,
      "time": {
        "type": "time",
        "count": 1,
        "unit": "day"
      },
      "cost": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "potent medicine valued at 200 gp"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "primary": {
        "skills": ["skill:medicine"],
        "proficiency": "expert"
      },
      "secondary": {
        "checks": [
          {
            "skills": ["skill:nature"]
          },
          {
            "skills": ["skill:religion"]
          }
        ],
        "casters": 1
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "001cd54e-67ea-53d1-aadf-434939c4af1e",
    "pack": "tian-xia-world-guide",
    "kind": "ritual",
    "slug": "ritual:the-unseeing-blade-master",
    "name": "The Unseeing Blade Master",
    "level": 6,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["trial"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "tian-xia-world-guide"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "There are many legends of blade masters who, not wanting to rely on flawed mortal eyes, learned to fight through reliance on both their other keen senses and knowledge from the universe itself. Those who intentionally seek out the path often do so by running through forms in thick clouds of incense."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Making a Strike against an enemy you can see is anathema to this ritual and immediately ends its benefits. If the ritual is ended in this way, you must conduct an Atone ritual before attempting this ritual again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " As success, except you can instead defeat an enemy in single combat that both uses a sword and is higher level than you."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You call a blessing into your sword to guide you on the path and are bound by the ritual's anathema. Once you've used that sword against 20 enemies, each significant enough to grant XP, you gain the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "a7539372-4fec-53a0-8996-95d3194acd8c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " feat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The incense is dispersed by a strange gust of wind and you learn nothing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The sword you're intending to use for the ritual becomes broken. If you aren't permanently blind, you're instead "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "5d63458a-cde5-5d64-8fea-b920f04f36b7"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for 1 month and can't repeat this ritual during that time."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.5xf9wK9xyAeGFPw7"
    },
    "data": {
      "rank": 6,
      "time": {
        "type": "time",
        "count": 1,
        "unit": "day"
      },
      "cost": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "rare incense worth 1,500 gp"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "primary": {
        "text": "Perception (master)"
      },
      "secondary": {
        "checks": [
          {
            "skills": ["skill:religion", "skill:lore:warfare"]
          }
        ],
        "casters": 1
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "cd95fa35-3552-58ed-9ebd-4131165963d0",
    "pack": "tian-xia-world-guide",
    "kind": "ritual",
    "slug": "ritual:wild-allegiance",
    "name": "Wild Allegiance",
    "level": 3,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["trial"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "tian-xia-world-guide"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To many, the animals of Tian Xia are simply beasts to be conquered or harvested, but this isn't how all of the gods intended it. You approach, feed, and commune with the most notably hostile beasts in an effort to forge a true friendship and allegiance with the natural world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wantonly attacking or killing animals is anathema to this ritual and immediately ends its benefits. If the ritual is ended in this way, you must conduct an Atone ritual before attempting this ritual again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " As success, except you can instead resolve a conflict with one animal of level 15 or higher."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You declare your allegiance to the wild and are bound by the ritual's anathema, but you still must prove yourself. Once you've nonviolently resolved conflicts with three different animals of a higher level than yours, you gain the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "e6799b06-142e-5f77-8d25-4f7c94a3fad6"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " feat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your actions don't impress the gods of the wilds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You deeply offend the gods you were trying to impress, and they send a sign of displeasure, often an animal attack. You must conduct an "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "atone",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " ritual before attempting this ritual again."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.BBw5oGFvoQc3gg52"
    },
